  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1254 AM MDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nThe monsoon plume continues funneling into our area on Friday, \nthough the best moisture tap will shift a bit further west. Most of \nthe precipitation for Friday will be over the mountains, with a \ncontinued chance for heavy rainfall and flash flooding. Meanwhile, \nsome afternoon showers and storms will be possible over the plains \nas well, but things further east will be more isolated. The \nexception to this will be the Palmer Divide, which should see some \nmore widespread rain thanks to a weak incoming cold front in the \nevening. Post-frontal upslope will make the plains a bit more active \non Saturday, with some lingering low-level moisture and instability \nthrough the afternoon hours. Another front will also move through \nsometime Saturday evening into early Sunday, which will help keep \nconvection going over the area.\n\nMeanwhile, drier air will work its way into the mountains as flow \naloft turns westerly on Sunday. The mountains will largely dry out, \nleaving some isolated-scattered activity over the plains in the \nafternoon hours. Meanwhile, the passing fronts will knock \ntemperatures down a few degrees for the weekend. By Sunday highs \nwill largely remain in the 70s over most of our CWA. Heading into \nnext week, cooler temperatures look to stick around, with the \nmonsoon moisture returning as an upper low moves onto the CA coast.",
